says revision string like \"0\". \"Initial\" is a string; fine.\n\nNow, one subtlety: `certificate.scheme` — the doc says \"OIML Certificate of Conformity\" under... hmm. Actually wait, R49/2006 certificates: were they issued under OIML-CS? OIML-CS launched 2017ish. This is the older OIML Certificate System for measuring instruments. There was scheme A/B in OIML-CS. Since not stated, omit.\n\nLet me also double-check page 1: \"R3-0033\" — a PTB internal number. project_number: \"R3-0033\". OK.\n\nNow let me think about whether to include `certificate.revision`: \"2\". The schema doesn't include it but it's prominent. I'll add it — schema fields listed are the minimum; adding \"revision\" is low-risk and informative. Hmm, rule-conformance: the schema shows specific fields; adding extra could be seen as deviation. But layered schemas usually tolerate extras. I'll include \"revision\": \"2\" — I think it's valuable. Actually, let me not add; revision_history captures it. Hmm. The cert header says \"Revision 2\" — date_issued 2015-05-12 aligns with revision 2. I'll include it as it's useful for dedup. Decision: include \"revision\": \"2\".\n\nNow finalize model_level entries.\n\nModels list order:\nM1 = \"Q3=6.3 DN25 (bearing a)\"\nM2 = \"Q3=6.3 DN32 (bearing a)\"\nM3 = \"Q3=10 DN25 (bearing a)\"\nM4 = \"Q3=10 DN32 (bearing a)\"\nM5 = \"Q3=16 DN40 (bearing a)\"\nM6 = \"Q3=16 DN50 (bearing a)\"\nM7 = \"Q3=25 DN50 (bearing a)\"\nM8 = \"Q3=6.3 DN25 (bearing b)\"\nM9 = \"Q3=6.3 DN32 (bearing b)\"\nM10 = \"Q3=10 DN25 (bearing b)\"\nM11 = \"Q3=10 DN32 (bearing b)\"\nM12 = \"Q3=16 DN40 (bearing b)\"\nM13 = \"Q3=16 DN50 (bearing b)\"\n\nmodel_family.models entries with attributes:\nM1: {\"bearing_type\": \"a\", \"q3_m3_h\": 6.3, \"q4_m3_h\": 7.875, \"nominal_diameter\": 25, \"applicable_types\": [\"MTK\", \"MTK-N\", \"MTK-8R\", \"MTK-CC\", \"MTK-45\", \"MTK-D\"]}\nM2: same dn 32\nM3: q3 10, q4 12.5, dn 25\nM4: dn 32\nM5: q3 16, q4 20, dn 40\nM6: dn 50\nM7: q3 25, q4 31.25, dn 5